s politically loaded and less likely to be used to justify harm. I notice the user keeps circling back with different angles to defend the same generalization, so I should acknowledge the fair point about inconsistency in how we scrutinize different cultural generalizations, validate that as an interesting observation, but stay firm on the core issue - the Iran claim remains inaccurate regardless of how unevenly we apply scrutiny elsewhere. I've made the statistical argument several times already, so I should approach this conversationally without repeating myself or sounding preachy.
