ral generalizations versus others—and if anything, that should push toward scrutinizing *all* of them more evenly, including the French wine one, rather than deciding the Persian smoking one gets a pass too. Inconsistent treatment of stereotypes doesn't validate the less-scrutinized one; it just means we're being sloppy across the board.
